In article <2kg2ke$s1i@eagle.lerc.nasa.gov>, fsctc@avelon.lerc.nasa.gov (Clarence Chang) writes:
>What is an Archon?  Is it any good as a pet?  How can I tame it?

Archons are very nasty.  It's one of the few things that has half a 
chance to kill a high level character.  They often weild some artifact 
as a weapon.  It is (arguably) the best pet.  They are very difficult 
to tame -- usually a scroll/spell of taming won't work on them.  The 
best way to get one is to wish for a blessed figurine of an Archon, 
and apply it on a vacant space.

>How does it compare with a Gray Dragon?

Just for fun I put an tame Archon in a small room with four gray dragons.
In a few turns, there were no more gray dragons.
